{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>He divided against them.</b> As a stratagem, so that they would think that all the surrounding peoples had risen against them — as Aram thought when they said: הִנֵּה שָׂכַר עָלֵינוּ מֶלֶךְ יִשְׂרָאֵל (II Kings 7:6)." "<b>By night.</b> This too was part of his stratagem, so that they would not see that they were few — as Ahithophel counseled when he said: וְאֶרְדְּפָה אַחֲרֵי דָוִד הַלַּיְלָה (II Samuel 17:1)." "<b>He struck them.</b> A blow that induces them to flee." "<b>He pursued them.</b> For once they begin to fall, they are put to flight."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:05.896276242Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}